{
  "abstract": "Let u be a degree-2 function on an elliptic curve E in characteristic 0, let a be a constant with A = a² ∉ {0, −1}, and put h = (u² − 1)/a. A septuple of translates is a 6-set 𝒜 such that the seven functions {a} ∪ {h(P + s) : s ∈ 𝒜} are distinct and 1 + h(P + s)h(P + t) has even divisor for all s ≠ t in 𝒜. Under its hypotheses, Paper 95 showed that 𝒜 is a coset of Z/6 (type P1) or generates Z/2 × Z/4 (type P4), and conjectured that P4 does not occur. We prove there is no P4 septuple of translates when the edges at the two order-4 classes have option (i) (a constant times a square) or (ii) (proportional to the branch discriminant), with any 2-torsion edges and without Paper 95's hypotheses (H2), (H3). So under Paper 95's hypotheses every septuple of translates has type P1. A written argument shows that option (ii) forces u(P + T) = −u(P) for a 2-torsion point T, so two translates coincide. For option (i) at both classes, the two-edge lemma of Paper 95, in the projective form of Paper 96 (codex_arithmetic) that needs no (H2), (H3), puts the source in that family or in a family I_e with u(P + T_e) = ±κ/u(P), κ² = 1 + A. In I_e, nine Gröbner bases over Q (three 2-torsion points, three charts) give the unit ideal, each with a cofactor identity checked by separate SymPy and python-flint code. The 1125 stratum systems of the previous version remain as a check: Singular gives the unit ideal exactly on all but 24 of the 500 not covered by the written argument. Option (iii′) edges at order 4 and isolated rational septuples are open.",
